  "id": "COMPOUND:31255 - PROTEIN:861",
  "verbalization": "Bonducellin is implicated in the interaction with Retinoic acid receptor alpha through multiple pathways, all of which involve DNA polymerase alpha subunit B as a common intermediate. This subunit is targeted by three distinct compounds—5-Hydroxy-7-methoxy-3-[3,4,5-trihydroxy-6-(hydroxymethyl)oxan-2-yl]oxy-2-[4-[3,4,5-trihydroxy-6-(hydroxymethyl)oxan-2-yl]oxyphenyl]chromen-4-one, Phorbaketal A, and Ailanthoidol—each of which directly targets Retinoic acid receptor alpha. The shared target of these compounds suggests a potential mechanism by which Bonducellin may influence Retinoic acid receptor alpha, possibly through the inhibition of DNA polymerase alpha subunit B. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between Bonducellin and Retinoic acid receptor alpha, where the activation or inhibition of DNA polymerase alpha subunit B could serve as a critical step in the pathway. The consistent presence of DNA polymerase alpha subunit B as a target across these pathways strengthens the hypothesis that Bonducellin exerts its effects via this intermediate, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the exact mode of action.",
